Benny is a human child of nine in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], serious beyond his years and hard to one-up. He carries a heavy pick he calls an exemplar weapon, an aspect of himself. He keeps company with [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]] and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]].

He was killed in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]]. He came back, but left a piece of himself behind in the [[Pharos]] to be fetched later, and now bears Aut's hidden mark. He meant to kill the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] to honor [[People/Argyle|Argyle]].

[[Aut]] later called the piece of him left in the Pharos back into him, and he was whole again. He got the revenge he wanted: he and the others ambushed the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] in a Widdershins alley and killed him, and took his car.

He fought the Roundhats in the fane beneath the Gas-n-Go, and when his pick wounded Tywelwyn's burnt husk, the fire inside it burst out over him and Arctos.

In the armory below the fane he found a ring box holding two silver rings and copied Tywelwyn's blackboard map of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] before the shift crew arrived. In the ambush he killed the crocodile and the bear, and ran down the bat as it fled to its car. The Party took the crew's car, their third.

He picked the lock on [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]]'s flat, and in the fight that followed the [[Bestiary/Cairn White|cairn white]] drained him and knocked him down. Afterwards he wiped the room for fingerprints. At the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Convox]] he asked where the police post contracts for freelancers, and the desk told him they do not, and that Brooks had hired the Party himself. That night he walked out in his pyjamas to the fax machine and said he had to re-up his permission slip sometimes.

At the parking-lot sale he kept the group's money and afterwards bought a rapier. At the cabin at void 26 he unbolted the bed Anaïs was chained to, and the shackle opened at his touch as it did for Arctos and Johnny. He asked Anaïs whether he was made of metal.

Before the pilgrimage he bought a plain fitted suit to wear to it. He drove the Party out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], and at a rest-stop gas station on the way he was too caught up in a question to notice the ambush until it began. He fought the robbers with his pick, searched their van, and found a plasma rifle and about 135 gold in small bills they had taken off other travelers.

At the pilgrimage he was handed a gorilla mask, one of the plain white ones, and wore it through the night.

In the disused train yard the wheel landed on red and put three [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] and a [[Bestiary/Brimorak|Brimorak]] against the four of them. Benny stood in the middle of them and traded blows until he went down, and when he came to he killed the brimorak with his silver pick, and killed the last [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] as well. When it was over he was on the ground with his weapons dropped and a healing potion in each hand, and he and the others bled from wounds that would not close until they saw to them.

At the pilgrimage he took the dice table with Johnny, betting fifty gold on the game and flipping a die to a four behind Johnny's distracting backflip, and won a hundred gold and a hint. He gave his name as Bennix Plasmadio to the majordomo at the Vane manor and again for a guest pass at the Belvedere library.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] he worked the reference shelves with [[People/Anzu|Anzu]], chasing whatever the papers held on Prime Meridian and its Hearts. At [[Org/The Undertable/index|the Undertable]] he bought a falcata from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]]. He drove the Party to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus]] on Sunday, and on the way out caught their car's radio dial slipping on its own toward a dead frequency, then turned it on and followed the voice that gave them directions to the back of the building.
